-- חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ד/2 (16.8.2023): חוזר העסקת עו"ה, עובדי בעלות, בבתי ספר
-- לחינוך מיוחד מוכרים שאינם רשמיים, בהתאם לרפורמת אופק חדש בשנה"ל תשפ"ד.
-- Bringing the recognized unofficial special-education schools that have
-- not yet joined into Ofek Hadash from תשפ"ד: who does what and by when,
-- who joins, the work weeks (primary, post-primary, health professions),
-- part-time and over-100% employment, mothers' and age hours, principals
-- and deputies, school-activity hours, leaving the reform, seniority,
-- promotion, counselors, grade determination and role bonuses, trip escort
-- pay, salary advances, the attendance clock, and the annexes (the owner's
-- commitment, the forms, and the salary-conversion method).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

-- Time in this file's regulative rules is counted in DAYS from 16 August
-- 2023 (day 0), the circular's date.
`30 August 2023`   MEANS 14
`1 September 2023` MEANS 16
`31 August 2024`   MEANS 381

-- Two money helpers for the annex's worked examples: to the agora by
-- truncation, and to the agora rounded half up (amounts here are positive).
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `truncated to the agora` x IS TRUNC x 2

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `rounded to the agora` x IS TRUNC (x PLUS 0.005) 2

§ `חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ד/2`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, date, reference number, circular number, addressee (the owners of special-education schools in recognized unofficial education that have not yet joined Ofek Hadash), greeting and subject line; no rule.

@desc A school, as far as this circular asks about one.
DECLARE `tashpad 2 school` HAS
    `recognized unofficial special education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc a recognized unofficial (מוכר שאינו רשמי) school for special education, not a special-education class
    `already in Ofek Hadash`                  IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `role` IS ONE OF
    `teacher`
    `principal`
    `first deputy principal`
    `second or later deputy principal`
    `educational counselor`

DECLARE `school stage` IS ONE OF
    `primary special-education school`
    `post-primary special-education school`
    `multi-stage, grades 1-6`
    `multi-stage, grades 7 and up`

@desc A teaching employee of the owner, as far as this circular asks about one.
DECLARE `tashpad 2 teacher` HAS
    `teacher role`                    IS A `role`
    `academic`                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc holds an academic degree, or a salary grade the Ministry's teaching-staff division approved as equivalent to an academic one
    `certified to teach`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc holds a teaching certificate or certification
    `prior teaching years recognized` IS A NUMBER  @desc years of actual teaching recognized before (from a non-State employer or in State service), not counting an internship year or teaching in IDF or national service
    `teaching seniority`              IS A NUMBER  @desc years of teaching seniority
    `position fraction`               IS A NUMBER  @desc the share of a full position held (1 = 100%)
    `is an intern`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc in the internship (סטאז') year
    `approved as an exception`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc the exceptions committee approved joining without a teaching certificate (3.2)
    `of the health professions`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc an occupational therapist, physiotherapist or speech therapist, or an arts therapist
    `age`                             IS A NUMBER  @desc age, determined as before the reform (8.1)

§§ `1 מבוא`

-- akn:art_1/p1 akn:art_1/p2 akn:art_1/p3 akn:art_1/p4 akn:art_1/p5 akn:art_1/p6 The background: in HCJ 148/18 (WIZO v. Ministry of Education) the State undertook to equalize the teaching resources of recognized unofficial special-education schools with official ones from תש"ף; an inter-ministerial team reported (linked) and the reform's terms were applied to those schools from תש"ף; no rule of this circular's own.

-- ¶7-¶9: regulation 3(6) of the recognized-institutions regulations,
-- amended in 2022, sets the salaries in a special-education institution
-- (not a special-education class) by the rates and rules of official
-- special-education institutions in the new programme; so every
-- special-education institution not yet joined joins from תשפ"ד.
@ref akn:art_1/p7 akn:art_1/p8 akn:art_1/p9
GIVEN s IS A `tashpad 2 school`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `joins Ofek Hadash from תשפ"ד` s IF
        s's `recognized unofficial special education`
    AND NOT s's `already in Ofek Hadash`

-- ¶10: the Ministry alone approves a teacher's joining, sets the grade and
-- converts the salary; it also sets the education level and seniority.
@ref akn:art_1/p10
DECLARE `determination` IS ONE OF
    `approving a teacher's joining`
    `setting the Ofek Hadash grade`
    `converting the salary`
    `setting the education level`
    `setting teaching seniority`

GIVEN d IS A `determination`
GIVETH A `Party`
DECIDE `who determines` d IS `the Ministry of Education`

-- akn:art_1/p11 The circular's purpose: to set out the instructions for the owners' teachers in these schools for תשפ"ד; the instructions follow.

§§ `2 תחומי אחריות ביישום הרפורמה`

-- akn:art_2 The heading of section 2; no rule.
-- akn:art_2__para_2-1 akn:art_2__para_2-1/p2 The headings "שלב ראשון" (stage one) and "פעולות המתבצעות ע"י הבעלות" (the owner's actions); no rule.

DECLARE `tashpad 2 action` IS ONE OF
    `submit the commitment letter`
    `verify and update the teachers' data`
    `have unreported teachers open an online file`
    `employ by the Ofek Hadash terms`
    `guide teachers to open an online file`
    `set the timetable by the Ofek Hadash work week`
    `place every teacher in the placement system`
    `send the salary interface to the contractor`
    `pay by the determined grade and offset the advances`
    `set the Ofek Hadash grade`
    `reimburse the owner`
    `install an attendance clock`
    `report hours by the attendance clock`
    `pay and deduct by the attendance reports`
    `apply the Ofek Hadash agreement`

-- 2.1(1): the owner signs the commitment of annex א and sends it by e-mail;
-- the last day is 30.8.2023.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p3 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p4 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_1/p5
GIVEN s IS A `tashpad 2 school`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 2 action`
DECIDE `the commitment letter` s IS
    IF `joins Ofek Hadash from תשפ"ד` s
    THEN PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         MUST  `submit the commitment letter`
         WITHIN `30 August 2023`
         LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "circular תשפ\"ד/2 2.1(1): the last day to send the commitment letter is 30.8.2023"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- 2.1(2): the teaching-staff report in the עוש"ר system lists the teachers
-- as reported. (א) the owner must make sure the data (academic and
-- pedagogic education, seniorities, training credits, double degree) are
-- current, and have them updated through the district (a contact person is
-- suggested). (ג) after stage א, find the teachers who meet the joining
-- conditions (section 3).
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_a akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_a/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_c
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 2 action`
DECIDE `the teachers' data are kept current` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `verify and update the teachers' data`
    WITHIN `1 September 2023`
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "circular תשפ\"ד/2 2.1(2)(א): the owner must make sure the teachers' data are current"

-- 2.1(2)(ב): teachers not yet reported — health professions and arts
-- therapists included — are told to open an online file urgently (link);
-- the steps follow the circular on employment approval (link).
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b/p3 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b/p4 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_2__cls_b/p5
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 2 action`
DECIDE `unreported teachers open a file` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `have unreported teachers open an online file`
    WITHIN `1 September 2023`
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "circular תשפ\"ד/2 2.1(2)(ב): unreported teachers must open an online file urgently"

-- 2.1(3): the teachers who meet the joining conditions are employed on Ofek
-- Hadash's salary terms and work week, as updated by the 2022 agreement and
-- before (section 4).
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_3
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 2 teacher`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 2 action`
DECIDE `employment by the Ofek Hadash terms` t IS
    IF `joins Ofek Hadash` t
    THEN PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         MUST  `employ by the Ofek Hadash terms`
         WITHIN `1 September 2023`
         LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "circular תשפ\"ד/2 2.1(3): a teacher who meets the joining conditions is employed on Ofek Hadash's terms"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- 2.1(3) ¶2 and 1-3, the principal: guide teachers without a file (health
-- professions and arts therapists included) to open an online file; set
-- the reform teachers' timetable by the Ofek Hadash week (section 4);
-- place every teacher — in the reform or not — in the placement system.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_3/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_3__cls_1 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_3__cls_2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__subpara_3__cls_3
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 2 action`
DECIDE `the principal's stage-one actions` IS
    (PARTY `the school principal` MUST `guide teachers to open an online file` WITHIN `1 September 2023`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the school principal` MUST `set the timetable by the Ofek Hadash work week` WITHIN `1 September 2023`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the school principal` MUST `place every teacher in the placement system` WITHIN `1 September 2023`)

-- 2.2 and (1)-(2): the owner sends the supplier (Unique) an interface of the
-- salary paid in the month requested; the Ministry sets the grade and
-- converts; once reported back, the owner pays by the grade from the
-- joining date and offsets the advances.
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_02-a: the advances are said to be "כאמור בסעיף 15
-- להלן"; section 15 is grade determination, and the advances are section 17.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-2 akn:art_2__para_2-2/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_1 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 2 action`
DECIDE `stage two` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `send the salary interface to the contractor`
    WITHIN `31 August 2024`
    HENCE (PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
           MUST  `set the Ofek Hadash grade`
           WITHIN `31 August 2024`
           HENCE (PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
                  MUST  `pay by the determined grade and offset the advances`
                  WITHIN `31 August 2024`))

`the section 2.2 says the advances are in` MEANS 15
`the section the advances are in` MEANS 17
`the grade-determination section` MEANS 15

`2.2's reference to the advances points at grade determination` MEANS
        `the section 2.2 says the advances are in` EQUALS `the grade-determination section`
    AND NOT (`the section 2.2 says the advances are in` EQUALS `the section the advances are in`)
#ASSERT `2.2's reference to the advances points at grade determination`

-- 2.2 ¶2-¶11: the Ministry (1) joins the schools once the commitment is in
-- and marks them; (2) checks each teacher against the joining conditions
-- after the תשפ"ד position is reported; (3) sets the grades; (4) computes
-- the schools' Ofek Hadash profile; (5) reimburses the owner — but without
-- the placement system updated to the Ofek Hadash week and the salary
-- interface sent, it cannot reimburse.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p3 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p4 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p5 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p6 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p7 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p8 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p9 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p10 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p11
GIVEN `placement updated and interface sent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 2 action`
DECIDE `the Ministry's stage-two actions` `placement updated and interface sent` IS
    IF `placement updated and interface sent`
    THEN (PARTY `the Ministry of Education` MUST `set the Ofek Hadash grade` WITHIN `31 August 2024`)
         RAND
         (PARTY `the Ministry of Education` MUST `reimburse the owner` WITHIN `31 August 2024`)
    ELSE PARTY `the Ministry of Education` MUST `set the Ofek Hadash grade` WITHIN `31 August 2024`

§§ `3 תנאי ההצטרפות`

-- akn:art_3 The heading of section 3; no rule.
-- akn:art_3__para_3-1 The heading "הגדרות" (definitions); no rule.

-- 3.1.1 a new teaching employee: no years of actual teaching recognized
-- before (internship, IDF or national-service teaching aside). 3.1.2 an
-- existing one: entitled to recognition of years of actual teaching.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_3-1-1
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 2 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a new teaching employee` t IF
    t's `prior teaching years recognized` EQUALS 0

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_3-1-2
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 2 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an existing teaching employee` t IF
    t's `prior teaching years recognized` GREATER THAN 0

-- akn:art_3__para_3-2 akn:art_3__para_3-2/p2 The headings of 3.2 (joining conditions of existing teachers) and "עו"ה קיימים אקדמאים"; no rule.

-- 3.2 ¶3-¶7: an existing academic in a joined institution joins if
-- certified to teach and employed at a third of a position or more.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-2/p3 akn:art_3__para_3-2/p4 akn:art_3__para_3-2/p5 akn:art_3__para_3-2/p6 akn:art_3__para_3-2/p7
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 2 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing academic meets the conditions` t IF
        t's `certified to teach`
    AND t's `position fraction` AT LEAST (1 DIVIDED BY 3)

-- 3.2 ¶8-¶9: one without a teaching certificate may apply, as an exception,
-- to the exceptions committee on annex ב's form, by e-mail.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-2/p8 akn:art_3__para_3-2/p9
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 2 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an uncertified academic joins as an exception` t IF
        NOT t's `certified to teach`
    AND t's `approved as an exception`

-- 3.2 ¶10-¶11: without a certificate and with under 25 years, no promotion
-- until certified; work and part of the studies count "as in 12.2.2".
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_02-b: section 12.2 has no 12.2.2; the rule is 13.2.2.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-2/p10 akn:art_3__para_3-2/p11
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 2 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `barred from advancing until certified under 3.2` t IF
        NOT t's `certified to teach`
    AND t's `teaching seniority` LESS THAN 25

`the subsections section 12.2 has` MEANS EMPTY
`3.2's reference to 12.2.2 has no target` MEANS
    NOT elem "12.2.2" `the subsections section 12.2 has`
#ASSERT `3.2's reference to 12.2.2 has no target`

-- akn:art_3__para_3-3 The heading of 3.3 (existing non-academics); no rule.

-- 3.3.1-3.3.2: an existing non-academic with 28 years or more is employed
-- on the reform's terms in any case; with fewer, not.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-1 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-2
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 2 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing non-academic joins` t IF
    t's `teaching seniority` AT LEAST 28

-- akn:art_3__para_3-4 The heading of 3.4 (joining new teachers to Ofek Hadash); no rule.

DECLARE `salary table` IS ONE OF
    `the bachelor's degree table`
    `the master's degree table`
    `a table by education (senior, certified or uncertified)`
    `no table`

DECLARE `degree` IS ONE OF `bachelor's`, `master's`, `doctorate`, `no degree`

-- 3.4.1: a new academic in a joined institution is placed at grade 1,
-- seniority 1: a BA in the BA table, an MA in the MA table, a doctorate in
-- the MA table with a 5% supplement on the combined salary.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-4__subpara_3-4-1 akn:art_3__para_3-4__subpara_3-4-1/p2 akn:art_3__para_3-4__subpara_3-4-1/p3 akn:art_3__para_3-4__subpara_3-4-1/p4 akn:art_3__para_3-4__subpara_3-4-1/p5
GIVEN d IS A `degree`
GIVETH A `salary table`
DECIDE `the table a new academic is placed in` d IS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `bachelor's` THEN `the bachelor's degree table`
    WHEN `master's` THEN `the master's degree table`
    WHEN `doctorate` THEN `the master's degree table`
    WHEN `no degree` THEN `no table`

`the starting grade of a new academic` MEANS 1
`the starting seniority of a new academic` MEANS 1

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-4__subpara_3-4-1/p6
GIVEN d IS A `degree`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the doctorate supplement rate` d IS
    IF d EQUALS `doctorate` THEN 0.05 ELSE 0

-- 3.4.2: new non-academic teachers not entitled to an intern's salary
-- (sections 145-148 of the Ofek Hadash agreement) are placed in the salary
-- tables by education (senior, certified or uncertified).
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_02-l: the paragraph sits under "joining new teachers to
-- Ofek Hadash" and does not say whether they join; the classes are the
-- pre-reform ones. The reading adopted: they do not join (as 3.3.2 says of
-- existing non-academics) and are placed by education.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-4__subpara_3-4-2
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 2 teacher`
GIVETH A `salary table`
DECIDE `the table a new non-academic is placed in` t IS
    `a table by education (senior, certified or uncertified)`

GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 2 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a new non-academic joins if 3.4.2 is a joining rule` t IF
    `is a new teaching employee` t AND NOT t's `is an intern`

`3.4.2 leaves open whether new non-academics join the reform` MEANS
    NOT (`a new non-academic joins if 3.4.2 is a joining rule` `a new non-academic teacher`
         EQUALS `joins Ofek Hadash` `a new non-academic teacher`)
#ASSERT `3.4.2 leaves open whether new non-academics join the reform`

-- akn:art_3__para_3-5 The heading of 3.5 (interns); no rule.

-- 3.5.1: interns are employed only on the reform's terms; the year counts
-- only at a third of a position or more.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-1
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 2 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the internship year is recognized` t IF
        t's `is an intern`
    AND t's `position fraction` AT LEAST (1 DIVIDED BY 3)

-- 3.5.2: at most two years, in which a degree and a teaching certificate
-- must be completed, or the intern may not stay on the reform's terms.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-2
GIVEN `years in internship` IS A NUMBER, `completed degree and certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an intern may stay on the reform's terms` `years in internship` `completed degree and certificate` IF
    `years in internship` AT MOST 2 OR `completed degree and certificate`

DECLARE `seniority purpose` IS ONE OF
    `salary seniority`
    `the minimum period for promotion`
    `tenure`
    `the jubilee grant`
    `recuperation`

-- 3.5.3: the internship does not count for salary seniority or the minimum
-- period for promotion; it counts for tenure, the jubilee grant and
-- recuperation.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-3
GIVEN p IS A `seniority purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the internship counts for` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `salary seniority` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the minimum period for promotion` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-4 akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-4/p2 akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-4/p3 A link to the details of interns' evaluation; no rule.
-- akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-5 akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-5/p2 akn:art_3__para_3-5__subpara_3-5-5/p3 A link to the map of dimensions for evaluating interns; no rule.

-- Who joins Ofek Hadash in a joined institution, by 3.2-3.5.
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 2 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `joins Ofek Hadash` t IF
    BRANCH IF t's `is an intern` THEN TRUE
           IF `is a new teaching employee` t THEN t's `academic`
           IF t's `academic` THEN `an existing academic meets the conditions` t OR `an uncertified academic joins as an exception` t
           OTHERWISE `an existing non-academic joins` t

`a new non-academic teacher` MEANS
    `tashpad 2 teacher` WITH
        `teacher role`                    IS `teacher`
        `academic`                        IS FALSE
        `certified to teach`              IS TRUE
        `prior teaching years recognized` IS 0
        `teaching seniority`              IS 0
        `position fraction`               IS 0.8
        `is an intern`                    IS FALSE
        `approved as an exception`        IS FALSE
        `of the health professions`       IS FALSE
        `age`                             IS 25

-- akn:art_3__para_3-6 The heading of 3.6 (substitute teachers); no rule.

-- 3.6: a substitute employed in weekly hours (not single hours), in the
-- reform or not, is employed on the terms of the teacher replaced.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-6/p2
GIVEN `employed in weekly hours` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the reform as the replaced teacher is` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a substitute is on the reform's terms` `employed in weekly hours` `in the reform as the replaced teacher is` IF
    `employed in weekly hours` AND `in the reform as the replaced teacher is`

§§ `4 מבנה שבוע העבודה למורים ברפורמה`

-- akn:art_4 The heading of section 4; no rule.

-- 4.1: a full-position teaching employee works 5 days a week, also in
-- schools that work 6.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-1
`the work days of a full position` MEANS 5

@desc A full-position weekly work structure, in hours.
DECLARE `work week` HAS
    `week total`      IS A NUMBER
    `week frontal`    IS A NUMBER
    `week individual` IS A NUMBER
    `week stay`       IS A NUMBER

-- 4.2: a teacher in a primary special-education school (grades 1-6, 1-8 or
-- 1-9), existing teachers on the 30-hour primary base or kept on the
-- 24-hour junior-high base included, works the primary special-education
-- week (4.4). 4.3: in a multi-stage special-education school, grades 1-6
-- (the 24-hour base kept included) work the primary week (4.4), grades
-- 7-12 the junior-high (post-primary) week (4.6).
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-2 akn:art_4__para_4-2/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-3 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-3/p4
GIVEN s IS A `school stage`, `of the health professions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the week of` s `of the health professions` IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `primary special-education school` THEN `the primary week for` `of the health professions`
    WHEN `multi-stage, grades 1-6` THEN `the primary week for` `of the health professions`
    OTHERWISE `the post-primary week for` `of the health professions`

-- akn:art_4__para_4-4 The heading of 4.4 (the primary special-education work week); no rule.

-- 4.4.1-4.4.4: 36 hours: 26 frontal, 5 individual (groups of up to 3
-- pupils, content set by the principal), 5 stay hours.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-1 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-2 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-3 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4
`the primary special-education week` MEANS `work week` WITH
    `week total`      IS 36
    `week frontal`    IS 26
    `week individual` IS 5
    `week stay`       IS 5

`the largest individual-hours group` MEANS 3

-- 4.4.4(1)-(2): work meetings take up to 2 stay hours a week; the rest go to
-- adapting the curriculum, meeting parents, marking, committees, guiding
-- the assistants, coordination with outside bodies and continuity; ¶9-¶11
-- link the detailed table.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p4 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p5 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p6 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p7 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p8 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p9 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p10 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2/p11 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_1 akn:art_4__para_4-4__subpara_4-4-4__cls_2
`the most primary stay hours for work meetings` MEANS 2

-- 4.5: health-profession teachers and arts therapists in a primary
-- special-education school: 3 individual hours and 7 stay hours (two of
-- which may go to moving between institutions); ¶3-¶5 link the table.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-5 akn:art_4__para_4-5/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-5/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-5/p4 akn:art_4__para_4-5/p5
`the primary health-professions week` MEANS `work week` WITH
    `week total`      IS 36
    `week frontal`    IS 26
    `week individual` IS 3
    `week stay`       IS 7

GIVEN `of the health professions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the primary week for` `of the health professions` IS
    IF `of the health professions` THEN `the primary health-professions week` ELSE `the primary special-education week`

-- akn:art_4__para_4-6 The heading of 4.6 (the post-primary work week); no rule.

-- 4.6.1-4.6.4: 36 hours: 23 frontal, 4 individual (groups of up to 3), 9
-- stay hours; work meetings up to 4; ¶11-¶13 link the table.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-1 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-2 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-3 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_1 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p4 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p5 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p6 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p7 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p8 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p9 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p10 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p11 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p12 akn:art_4__para_4-6__subpara_4-6-4__cls_2/p13
`the post-primary special-education week` MEANS `work week` WITH
    `week total`      IS 36
    `week frontal`    IS 23
    `week individual` IS 4
    `week stay`       IS 9

`the most post-primary stay hours for work meetings` MEANS 4

-- 4.7: health-profession teachers and arts therapists in a post-primary
-- special-education school: 2 individual hours and 11 stay hours (two for
-- moving between institutions); ¶3-¶5 link the table.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-7 akn:art_4__para_4-7/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-7/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-7/p4 akn:art_4__para_4-7/p5
`the post-primary health-professions week` MEANS `work week` WITH
    `week total`      IS 36
    `week frontal`    IS 23
    `week individual` IS 2
    `week stay`       IS 11

`the stay hours that may go to moving between institutions` MEANS 2

GIVEN `of the health professions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the post-primary week for` `of the health professions` IS
    IF `of the health professions` THEN `the post-primary health-professions week` ELSE `the post-primary special-education week`

GIVEN w IS A `work week`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the week adds up` w IF
    w's `week frontal` PLUS w's `week individual` PLUS w's `week stay` EQUALS w's `week total`

#ASSERT all `the week adds up` (LIST `the primary special-education week`, `the primary health-professions week`, `the post-primary special-education week`, `the post-primary health-professions week`)

§§ `5 העסקה בחלקיות משרה ברפורמה`

-- akn:art_5 The heading of section 5; no rule.

-- 5.1: no less than a third of a position. 5.2: a new teacher (not an
-- intern) at least 70%, and from 1.9.2024 at least 80%; an intern and an
-- existing teacher at least a third. 5.3: a health-profession teacher may
-- work below a third.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-1 akn:art_5__para_5-2 akn:art_5__para_5-2/p2 akn:art_5__para_5-3
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 2 teacher`, `from 1.9.2024` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the minimum position` t `from 1.9.2024` IS
    IF t's `of the health professions`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `is a new teaching employee` t AND NOT t's `is an intern`
         THEN IF `from 1.9.2024` THEN 0.8 ELSE 0.7
         ELSE 1 DIVIDED BY 3

-- 5.4: a part-time position is cut proportionally across frontal,
-- individual and stay hours.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-4
GIVEN w IS A `work week`, f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the part-time week` w f IS
    `work week` WITH
        `week total`      IS w's `week total` TIMES f
        `week frontal`    IS w's `week frontal` TIMES f
        `week individual` IS w's `week individual` TIMES f
        `week stay`       IS w's `week stay` TIMES f

-- 5.4 ¶2: a health-profession teacher, or one in a required subject by the
-- division's special approval, below a third of a position and at three
-- frontal hours or fewer ("single frontal hours"), teaches only those
-- hours, with no individual or stay hours; the position is those hours
-- over the position base.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-4/p2
GIVEN `frontal hours` IS A NUMBER, `position base` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the week of single frontal hours` `frontal hours` `position base` IS
    `work week` WITH
        `week total`      IS `frontal hours`
        `week frontal`    IS `frontal hours`
        `week individual` IS 0
        `week stay`       IS 0

GIVEN `frontal hours` IS A NUMBER, `position base` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position of single frontal hours` `frontal hours` `position base` IS
    `frontal hours` DIVIDED BY `position base`

-- 5.5: no more than two schools, and the total position no more than 100%;
-- not for health professions nor for a subject the division allowed in
-- more than two schools.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-5
GIVEN `number of schools` IS A NUMBER, `total position` IS A NUMBER, `exempt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `5.5 permits the employment` `number of schools` `total position` `exempt` IF
    `exempt`
    OR (`number of schools` AT MOST 2 AND `total position` AT MOST 1)

-- 5.6: employment below a third of a position does not count for the
-- required period (פז"נ) for promotion.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-6
GIVEN `position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the period counts for promotion` `position` IF
    `position` AT LEAST (1 DIVIDED BY 3)

§§ `6 העסקה מעל 100% משרה ברפורמה`

-- akn:art_6 The heading of section 6; no rule.

-- 6.1: as a rule up to 100%; above it only exceptionally, for teaching
-- employees (not principals or first deputies); the extra hours are
-- frontal only; at most 8.5 hours a day and 42 a week.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-1 akn:art_6__para_6-1/p2 akn:art_6__para_6-1/p3 akn:art_6__para_6-1/p4
GIVEN r IS A `role`, `daily hours` IS A NUMBER, `weekly hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be employed above 100%` r `daily hours` `weekly hours` IF
        NOT (r EQUALS `principal` OR r EQUALS `first deputy principal`)
    AND `daily hours` AT MOST 8.5
    AND `weekly hours` AT MOST 42

DECLARE `approval for over-100% employment` IS ONE OF
    `the principal approves, no request`
    `no approval needed`
    `a request in the entitlements system`

-- 6.2: in one institution the principal may approve up to 42 weekly hours
-- without a request. 6.3: two institutions up to 106% without approval.
-- 6.4: above 106% in two institutions, a request is filed.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-2 akn:art_6__para_6-3 akn:art_6__para_6-4
GIVEN `number of institutions` IS A NUMBER, `total position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `approval for over-100% employment`
DECIDE `the approval needed` `number of institutions` `total position` IS
    IF `number of institutions` EQUALS 1
    THEN `the principal approves, no request`
    ELSE IF `total position` AT MOST 1.06
         THEN `no approval needed`
         ELSE `a request in the entitlements system`

-- F-2023-24_tashpad_02-c: 5.5 caps two schools at 100%; 6.3 allows 106%
-- without approval. The reading adopted: section 6 is the exception.
`5.5 and 6.3 disagree on 104% in two schools` MEANS
        NOT `5.5 permits the employment` 2 1.04 FALSE
    AND `the approval needed` 2 1.04 EQUALS `no approval needed`
#ASSERT `5.5 and 6.3 disagree on 104% in two schools`

-- akn:art_6__para_6-4/p2 akn:art_6__para_6-4/p3 A pointer to the procedure for employment above 100% in recognized unofficial education for תשפ"ד; no rule.

§§ `7 משרת הורה`

-- akn:art_7 The heading of section 7; no rule.

-- 7.1: a mother's position per the takanon: a whole position of 79% or more.
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-1 akn:art_7__para_7-1/p2
GIVEN `position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to a mother's position` `position` IF
    `position` AT LEAST 0.79

@desc A weekly reduction of hours, by kind.
DECLARE `hours reduction` HAS
    `frontal reduction`    IS A NUMBER
    `individual reduction` IS A NUMBER
    `stay reduction`       IS A NUMBER

`no reduction` MEANS `hours reduction` WITH
    `frontal reduction`    IS 0
    `individual reduction` IS 0
    `stay reduction`       IS 0

-- 7.2: a mother cuts one frontal and one stay hour; the tables show it.
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-2 akn:art_7__para_7-2/p2
`a mother's reduction` MEANS `hours reduction` WITH
    `frontal reduction`    IS 1
    `individual reduction` IS 0
    `stay reduction`       IS 1

-- 7.3: after maternity leave, at 90% or more, for four months: 5 weekly
-- stay hours off (nursing), pay and position unchanged; 7.2 not then.
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-3
`a nursing reduction` MEANS `hours reduction` WITH
    `frontal reduction`    IS 0
    `individual reduction` IS 0
    `stay reduction`       IS 5

-- 7.4: at 79% to 90%, the mother's reduction of 7.2. 7.5: never both.
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_02-d: at exactly 90% both 7.3 and 7.4 apply. The
-- reading adopted: 7.3 governs at 90%.
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-4 akn:art_7__para_7-5
GIVEN `position` IS A NUMBER, `within four months of maternity leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `hours reduction`
DECIDE `the mother's reduction` `position` `within four months of maternity leave` IS
    IF `within four months of maternity leave` AND `position` AT LEAST 0.9
    THEN `a nursing reduction`
    ELSE IF `entitled to a mother's position` `position`
         THEN `a mother's reduction`
         ELSE `no reduction`

GIVEN `position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `hours reduction`
DECIDE `the reductions 7.3 and 7.4 give after maternity leave` `position` IS
    append (IF `position` AT LEAST 0.9 THEN LIST `a nursing reduction` ELSE EMPTY)
           (IF `position` AT LEAST 0.79 AND `position` AT MOST 0.9 THEN LIST `a mother's reduction` ELSE EMPTY)

`7.3 and 7.4 both take a 90% position` MEANS
    count (`the reductions 7.3 and 7.4 give after maternity leave` 0.9) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `7.3 and 7.4 both take a 90% position`

§§ `8 מורים הזכאים לשעות גיל`

-- akn:art_8 The heading of section 8; no rule.

-- 8.1: the age of eligibility is determined as before the reform.
@ref akn:art_8__para_8-1
`age eligibility is determined as before the reform` MEANS TRUE

@desc The age reduction for a full position, and the position base it leaves.
DECLARE `age hours` HAS
    `age frontal reduction`    IS A NUMBER
    `age individual reduction` IS A NUMBER
    `position base`            IS A NUMBER

-- 8.2: aged 50-55, 2 frontal hours off (part-time proportionally), base 34.
-- 8.3: existing teachers 55 and over, 3 frontal and 1 individual, base 32.
-- 8.4: new teachers 55 and over, 2 frontal only, base 34, nothing further.
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_02-e: an existing teacher aged 55 is in 8.2 and in 8.3.
-- The reading adopted: 8.3 governs at 55.
@ref akn:art_8__para_8-2 akn:art_8__para_8-3 akn:art_8__para_8-4 akn:art_8__para_8-4/p2
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 2 teacher`
GIVETH AN `age hours`
DECIDE `the age hours of` t IS
    IF t's `age` AT LEAST 55 AND `is an existing teaching employee` t
    THEN `age hours` 3 1 32
    ELSE IF t's `age` AT LEAST 50
         THEN `age hours` 2 0 34
         ELSE `age hours` 0 0 36

GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 2 teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the frontal hours cut for age` t IS
    (`the age hours of` t)'s `age frontal reduction` TIMES min (t's `position fraction`) 1

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `age hours`
DECIDE `the age rows an existing teacher falls in` `age` IS
    append (IF `age` AT LEAST 50 AND `age` AT MOST 55 THEN LIST (`age hours` 2 0 34) ELSE EMPTY)
           (IF `age` AT LEAST 55 THEN LIST (`age hours` 3 1 32) ELSE EMPTY)

`8.2 and 8.3 both take an existing teacher aged 55` MEANS
    count (`the age rows an existing teacher falls in` 55) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `8.2 and 8.3 both take an existing teacher aged 55`

§§ `9 מבנה שבוע העבודה למנהלים וסגנים ראשונים`

-- akn:art_9 The heading of section 9; no rule.

-- 9.1: principal and first deputy at exactly 100%, 5 days. 9.2: the
-- principal's week is 40 hours, 6-9 of them frontal by complexity. 9.7:
-- the first deputy's week is 40 hours.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-1 akn:art_9__para_9-2 akn:art_9__para_9-7
`the position of a principal or first deputy` MEANS 1
`the principal's weekly hours` MEANS 40
`the first deputy's weekly hours` MEANS 40

-- 9.3-9.4: 8 complexity levels by the school-management index set the
-- hours and pay of principal and first deputy; in special education the
-- lowest level is 3.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-3 akn:art_9__para_9-4
`the number of complexity levels` MEANS 8
`the minimum complexity level in special education` MEANS 3

GIVEN `computed level` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the complexity level of a special-education school` `computed level` IS
    max `computed level` `the minimum complexity level in special education`

-- 9.5-9.6: computed in early May of the year before; for a new or growing
-- school in December of the year itself, at the minimum level until then,
-- with retroactive correction.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-5 akn:art_9__para_9-6
GIVEN `existed in May of the year before` IS A BOOLEAN, `growing school` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `when the complexity level is computed` `existed in May of the year before` `growing school` IS
    IF `existed in May of the year before` AND NOT `growing school`
    THEN "early May of the previous school year"
    ELSE "December of the school year, with the minimum level until then and a retroactive update"

@desc One printed row of a complexity table: the level and the frontal hours.
DECLARE `complexity row` HAS
    `row level`         IS A NUMBER
    `row frontal hours` IS A NUMBER

-- 9.6 ¶2-¶12: the principal's frontal hours by complexity level. The corpus
-- carries this table as lines of prose (a corpus defect); each line is
-- "hours level": 9 at 3, 8 at 4 and 5, 7 at 6 and 7, 6 at 8.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-6/p2 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p3 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p4 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p5 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p6 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p7 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p8 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p9 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p10 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p11 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p12
`the principal's frontal hours table` MEANS
    LIST `complexity row` 3 9,
         `complexity row` 4 8,
         `complexity row` 5 8,
         `complexity row` 6 7,
         `complexity row` 7 7,
         `complexity row` 8 6

-- akn:art_9__para_9-6/p13 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p14 A link to how the complexity level is computed; no rule.

-- 9.7.1-9.7.3's tables: the first deputy's frontal hours by complexity, in
-- a primary school (18-21), a post-primary school (9-11) and a multi-stage
-- school (13-15).
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-1 akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-1/t1
`the primary first deputy's table` MEANS
    LIST `complexity row` 3 21, `complexity row` 4 21, `complexity row` 5 20,
         `complexity row` 6 20, `complexity row` 7 19, `complexity row` 8 18

@ref akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-2 akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-2/t1
`the post-primary first deputy's table` MEANS
    LIST `complexity row` 3 11, `complexity row` 4 11, `complexity row` 5 11,
         `complexity row` 6 11, `complexity row` 7 9, `complexity row` 8 9

@ref akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-3 akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-3/t1
`the multi-stage first deputy's table` MEANS
    LIST `complexity row` 3 15, `complexity row` 4 15, `complexity row` 5 14,
         `complexity row` 6 14, `complexity row` 7 13, `complexity row` 8 13

GIVEN `table` IS A LIST OF `complexity row`
      `level` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the hours the table gives` `table` `level` IS
    map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row frontal hours`) (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row level` EQUALS `level`) `table`)

GIVEN `table` IS A LIST OF `complexity row`
      `lowest` IS A NUMBER
      `highest` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the table has one row per level 3-8 within` `table` `lowest` `highest` IF
        all (GIVEN l YIELD count (`the hours the table gives` `table` l) EQUALS 1) (LIST 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8)
    AND all (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row frontal hours` AT LEAST `lowest` AND r's `row frontal hours` AT MOST `highest`) `table`

#ASSERT `the table has one row per level 3-8 within` `the principal's frontal hours table` 6 9
#ASSERT `the table has one row per level 3-8 within` `the primary first deputy's table` 18 21
#ASSERT `the table has one row per level 3-8 within` `the post-primary first deputy's table` 9 11
#ASSERT `the table has one row per level 3-8 within` `the multi-stage first deputy's table` 13 15

-- 9.8: a second or later deputy works a teacher's week, the individual
-- hours going to the deputy's work.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-8
GIVEN s IS A `school stage`
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the week of a second deputy` s IS
    `the week of` s FALSE

-- 9.9-9.10: a principal or first deputy entitled to a mother's position,
-- or aged 50 or more, gets 2 weekly hours off the non-frontal hours, pay and
-- position unchanged.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-9 akn:art_9__para_9-10
GIVEN `entitled to a mother's position` IS A BOOLEAN, `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `a manager's non-frontal reductions` `entitled to a mother's position` `age` IS
    append (IF `entitled to a mother's position` THEN LIST 2 ELSE EMPTY)
           (IF `age` AT LEAST 50 THEN LIST 2 ELSE EMPTY)

-- 9.11-9.12: an existing non-academic principal with 1-27 years must
-- complete an academic education within 4 years of the move to keep the
-- post, and meanwhile is employed on the non-academic principals' terms;
-- with 28 or more, on those terms.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-11 akn:art_9__para_9-12
GIVEN `salary seniority` IS A NUMBER, `years since the school moved` IS A NUMBER, `completed a degree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a non-academic principal keeps the post` `salary seniority` `years since the school moved` `completed a degree` IF
    `salary seniority` AT LEAST 28
    OR `completed a degree`
    OR `years since the school moved` AT MOST 4

-- 9.13: by section 31.1 of the agreement of 19.10.2022, a principal's and
-- first deputy's salary is global.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-13 akn:art_9__para_9-13/p2
GIVEN r IS A `role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is paid a global salary` r IF
    r EQUALS `principal` OR r EQUALS `first deputy principal`

§§ `10 שעות פעילות בית ספרית`

-- akn:art_10 The heading of section 10; no rule.

DECLARE `school-activity hour` IS ONE OF
    `on the teacher's day off`
    `instead of a stay hour that day`
    `instead of a stay hour that is made up another day`

-- 10.1, 10.5-10.7: 125% of the hour value on top of pay; instead of a stay
-- hour, the stay hour's 100% is not paid; made up another day, it is.
@ref akn:art_10__para_10-1 akn:art_10__para_10-5 akn:art_10__para_10-6 akn:art_10__para_10-7
GIVEN h IS A `school-activity hour`, `hour value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `pay for a school-activity hour` h `hour value` IS
    CONSIDER h
    WHEN `on the teacher's day off` THEN 1.25 TIMES `hour value`
    WHEN `instead of a stay hour that day` THEN 1.25 TIMES `hour value` MINUS `hour value`
    WHEN `instead of a stay hour that is made up another day` THEN 1.25 TIMES `hour value`

-- 10.2-10.4: at most 40 hours a year, a pre-opening meeting of up to 3
-- included; the activities, allocated by the principal.
@ref akn:art_10__para_10-2 akn:art_10__para_10-3 akn:art_10__para_10-4
GIVEN `hours allocated` IS A NUMBER, `pre-opening hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the allocation is within the limits` `hours allocated` `pre-opening hours` IF
        `hours allocated` AT MOST 40
    AND `pre-opening hours` AT MOST 3
    AND `pre-opening hours` AT MOST `hours allocated`

§§ `11 יציאה מאופק חדש`

-- akn:art_11 The heading of section 11; no rule.

DECLARE `reason to leave` IS ONE OF
    `the health of the teacher or a first-degree relative, with current medical certificates`
    `a change for the worse in personal or family circumstances since joining`
    `another reason`

-- 11.1-11.2: as a rule every eligible teacher joins; exceptionally a
-- request to leave may be considered for health or humanitarian reasons.
@ref akn:art_11__para_11-2/p2 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p3 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p4 akn:art_11__para_11-1 akn:art_11__para_11-2
GIVEN r IS A `reason to leave`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a request to leave may be considered` r IF
    NOT (r EQUALS `another reason`)

-- 11.3-11.4: on annex ג's form, to the conditions-of-service officer by e-mail.
@ref akn:art_11__para_11-3 akn:art_11__para_11-4
`the form for a request to leave` MEANS "annex ג"

§§ `12 ותק בהוראה`

-- akn:art_12 The heading of section 12; no rule.

-- 12.1: recognized seniority is the takanon's teaching seniority without the
-- internship and compulsory IDF service, with IDF or national-service
-- teaching. 12.2: notwithstanding 12.1, an existing teacher keeps every
-- year recognized for salary before the move.
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-1
GIVEN `takanon teaching seniority` IS A NUMBER, `internship years in it` IS A NUMBER, `compulsory service years in it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `recognized seniority` `takanon teaching seniority` `internship years in it` `compulsory service years in it` IS
    `takanon teaching seniority` MINUS `internship years in it` MINUS `compulsory service years in it`

@ref akn:art_12__para_12-2
GIVEN `years recognized before the move` IS A NUMBER, `recognized seniority under 12.1` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `an existing teacher's recognized seniority` `years recognized before the move` `recognized seniority under 12.1` IS
    max `years recognized before the move` `recognized seniority under 12.1`

§§ `13 קידום בדרגות הערכה ופיתוח מקצועי`

-- akn:art_13 The heading of section 13; no rule.

@desc One printed row of a promotion table: from grade, to grade, the required months (פז"נ) and development hours (שפ"מ).
DECLARE `promotion step` HAS
    `from grade`      IS A STRING
    `to grade`        IS A STRING
    `required months` IS A NUMBER
    `required hours`  IS A NUMBER

-- 13.1: promotion requires the required period, development hours and an
-- evaluation by the Ministry's guidelines.
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-1 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p2 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p3 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p4
GIVEN `months in grade` IS A NUMBER, `development hours` IS A NUMBER, `evaluation passed` IS A BOOLEAN, s IS A `promotion step`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the promotion criteria` `months in grade` `development hours` `evaluation passed` s IF
        `months in grade` AT LEAST s's `required months`
    AND `development hours` AT LEAST s's `required hours`
    AND `evaluation passed`

-- akn:art_13__para_13-1/p5 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p6 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p7 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p8 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p9 Links to the evaluation for promotion and the map of indicators; no rule.
-- akn:art_13__para_13-2 The heading of 13.2 (teachers' promotion); no rule.

-- 13.2.1's table (¶2-¶3 are its header, split by the corpus): certified academics.
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-1 akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-1/p2 akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-1/p3 akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-1/t1
`the certified academics' promotion table` MEANS
    LIST `promotion step` "1" "2" 30 120,
         `promotion step` "2" "3" 30 120,
         `promotion step` "3" "4" 36 180,
         `promotion step` "4" "5" 36 180,
         `promotion step` "5" "6" 36 180,
         `promotion step` "6" "7" 48 210,
         `promotion step` "7" "8" 48 210,
         `promotion step` "8" "9" 48 210

-- akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-2 The heading of 13.2.2 (academics not certified to teach); no rule.

-- 13.2.2: veterans with "up to 25" years joining by exception may not
-- advance until certified (then the period counts from joining, for one
-- promotion, and up to 60 study hours count); "25 and more" need not
-- certify; new teachers joining by exception accrue from certification.
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_02-f: 25 years is in both rows. The reading adopted:
-- 25 is "25 and more" (as 3.2 bars only "below 25").
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-2/p2 akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-2/p3 akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-2/p4 akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-2/p5 akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-2/p6 akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-2/p7
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 2 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an uncertified academic may advance` t IF
    t's `certified to teach` OR (`is an existing teaching employee` t AND t's `teaching seniority` AT LEAST 25)

GIVEN `seniority` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF BOOLEAN
DECIDE `what 13.2.2's two rows say of advancing uncertified` `seniority` IS
    append (IF `seniority` AT MOST 25 THEN LIST FALSE ELSE EMPTY)
           (IF `seniority` AT LEAST 25 THEN LIST TRUE ELSE EMPTY)

`13.2.2 gives a teacher of exactly 25 years both answers` MEANS
    `what 13.2.2's two rows say of advancing uncertified` 25 EQUALS LIST FALSE, TRUE
#ASSERT `13.2.2 gives a teacher of exactly 25 years both answers`

-- akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-3 The heading of 13.2.3 (certified non-academics); no rule.

-- 13.2.3 ¶2: from 1.9.2023 sections 51, 59, 60 and 61 of the Ofek Hadash
-- agreement are cancelled, except for teachers who signed before 30.6.2023
-- a commitment to complete an academic education within four years.
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-3/p2
GIVEN `signed the four-year commitment before 30.6.2023` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sections 51, 59, 60 and 61 still apply from 1.9.2023` `signed the four-year commitment before 30.6.2023` IF
    `signed the four-year commitment before 30.6.2023`

-- 13.2.3 ¶3-¶5 and the table: certified non-academics with 28 years or
-- more need not complete an academic education.
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-3/p3 akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-3/p4 akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-3/p5 akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-3/t1
`the certified non-academics' promotion table` MEANS
    LIST `promotion step` "1" "2" 48 480,
         `promotion step` "2" "3" 48 480,
         `promotion step` "3" "4" 48 480,
         `promotion step` "4" "5" 48 480,
         `promotion step` "5" "6" 48 480,
         `promotion step` "6" "7" 48 480,
         `promotion step` "7" "8" 48 480,
         `promotion step` "8" "9" 48 480

-- akn:art_13__para_13-3 The heading of 13.3 (principals' and deputies' promotion); no rule.

@ref akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-1 akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-1/p2 akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-1/p3 akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-1/t1
`the academic managers' promotion table` MEANS
    LIST `promotion step` "א" "ב" 36 210,
         `promotion step` "ב" "ג" 36 210,
         `promotion step` "ג" "ד" 36 210

@ref akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2 akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2/p2 akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2/p3 akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2/t1
`the non-academic managers' promotion table` MEANS
    LIST `promotion step` "א" "ב" 48 480,
         `promotion step` "ב" "ג" 48 480,
         `promotion step` "ג" "ד" 48 480

§§ `14 יועצים חינוכיים`

-- akn:art_14 The heading of section 14; no rule.

-- 14.1: a counselor works an academic teacher's week, the frontal hours split
-- between teaching and counseling by the principal, the individual hours
-- counseling, the stay hours serving counseling too; at least 1/6 of the
-- position (6 of 36) frontal teaching in primary and junior high, and no
-- less than 4 frontal hours for any position.
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-1 akn:art_14__para_14-1/p2 akn:art_14__para_14-1/p3 akn:art_14__para_14-1/p4 akn:art_14__para_14-1/p5 akn:art_14__para_14-1/p6 akn:art_14__para_14-1/p7
GIVEN `position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a counselor's minimum frontal teaching hours` `position` IS
    max (36 TIMES `position` DIVIDED BY 6) 4

-- 14.2: new counselors are paid by the new academic combined-salary tables.
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-2
`the table new counselors are paid by` MEANS "the new combined-salary tables for academic teachers"

-- 14.3: at least 7 counseling hours earn the counseling bonus: 12% with a
-- temporary licence, 18% with a permanent one.
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-3 akn:art_14__para_14-3/p2 akn:art_14__para_14-3/p3
GIVEN `counseling hours` IS A NUMBER, `permanent licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the counseling bonus rate` `counseling hours` `permanent licence` IS
    IF `counseling hours` AT LEAST 7
    THEN IF `permanent licence` THEN 0.18 ELSE 0.12
    ELSE 0

§§ `15 קביעת הדרגה באופק חדש`

-- akn:art_15 The heading of section 15; no rule.

DECLARE `grade action` IS ONE OF
    `set a grade`

-- 15.1-15.5: the Ministry alone sets the grade, from employment, education
-- and salary data, converting by the March salary of the year before
-- joining (the salary due at 100% by the roles held); half grades allowed.
@ref akn:art_15__para_15-1 akn:art_15__para_15-2 akn:art_15__para_15-3 akn:art_15__para_15-4 akn:art_15__para_15-5
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `grade action`
DECIDE `only the Ministry sets grades` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    SHANT `set a grade`
    WITHIN `31 August 2024`
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "circular תשפ\"ד/2 15.1: the Ministry of Education alone sets Ofek Hadash grades"

`grades step in halves` MEANS 0.5

-- akn:art_15__para_15-6 akn:art_15__para_15-6/p2 akn:art_15__para_15-6/p3 akn:art_15__para_15-6/p4 akn:art_15__para_15-6/p5 akn:art_15__para_15-6/p6 akn:art_15__para_15-6/p7 Pointers: the grade-determination booklet, and links to the salary tables and the 2016 shekel and Ofek 2022 supplement circulars; no rule.

-- akn:art_15__para_15-7 The heading "גמולי תפקיד באופק חדש" (role bonuses); no rule.

@desc One printed role bonus: the role and its rate of the combined salary.
DECLARE `role bonus` HAS
    `bonus role` IS A STRING
    `bonus rate` IS A NUMBER

-- 15.7 ¶2-¶15 as printed: subject coordination and social education have a
-- primary and a junior-high rate; the grade coordinator's 7%/6% is by the
-- classes in the grade (15.8.2); the mentor's 2.4% is per intern, up to three.
@ref akn:art_15__para_15-7/p2 akn:art_15__para_15-7/p3 akn:art_15__para_15-7/p4 akn:art_15__para_15-7/p5 akn:art_15__para_15-7/p6 akn:art_15__para_15-7/p7 akn:art_15__para_15-7/p8 akn:art_15__para_15-7/p9 akn:art_15__para_15-7/p10 akn:art_15__para_15-7/p11 akn:art_15__para_15-7/p12 akn:art_15__para_15-7/p13 akn:art_15__para_15-7/p14 akn:art_15__para_15-7/p15
`the role bonuses` MEANS
    LIST `role bonus` "second deputy principal" 0.2,
         `role bonus` "class educator" 0.1,
         `role bonus` "first-grade class educator" 0.115,
         `role bonus` "subject coordinator, primary" 0.06,
         `role bonus` "subject coordinator, junior high" 0.08,
         `role bonus` "road-safety coordinator" 0.06,
         `role bonus` "security coordinator" 0.06,
         `role bonus` "social education, primary" 0.08,
         `role bonus` "social education, junior high" 0.1,
         `role bonus` "grade coordinator, up to 4 classes" 0.07,
         `role bonus` "grade coordinator, over 4 classes" 0.06,
         `role bonus` "laboratory coordinator" 0.03,
         `role bonus` "measurement and evaluation coordinator" 0.06,
         `role bonus` "trips coordinator" 0.06,
         `role bonus` "inclusion and integration coordinator" 0.06,
         `role bonus` "pedagogic coordinator" 0.06,
         `role bonus` "mentor, per intern" 0.024

-- ¶16: at most two role bonuses.
@ref akn:art_15__para_15-7/p16
GIVEN `rates of the roles held` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the role bonuses are within the limit` `rates of the roles held` IF
    count `rates of the roles held` AT MOST 2

-- ¶17-¶19 and א-ג, ג ¶2 and its א-ב: from 1.9.2023 (agreement of
-- 19.10.2022) the special-education bonus: certified, 9% to 10%, 14% to
-- 15%, autism or severe mental disorders classes 17%; not certified, 5.5%,
-- and 8.5% in special education.
@ref akn:art_15__para_15-7/p17 akn:art_15__para_15-7/p18 akn:art_15__para_15-7/p19 akn:art_15__para_15-7__subpara_a akn:art_15__para_15-7__subpara_b akn:art_15__para_15-7__subpara_c akn:art_15__para_15-7__subpara_c/p2 akn:art_15__para_15-7__subpara_c__cls_a akn:art_15__para_15-7__subpara_c__cls_b
GIVEN `certified in special education` IS A BOOLEAN, `rate before the agreement` IS A NUMBER, `autism or severe mental disorders class` IS A BOOLEAN, `in special education` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the special-education bonus from 1.9.2023` `certified in special education` `rate before the agreement` `autism or severe mental disorders class` `in special education` IS
    IF `certified in special education`
    THEN IF `rate before the agreement` EQUALS 0.14 AND `autism or severe mental disorders class`
         THEN 0.17
         ELSE IF `rate before the agreement` EQUALS 0.14
              THEN 0.15
              ELSE IF `rate before the agreement` EQUALS 0.09 THEN 0.1 ELSE `rate before the agreement`
    ELSE IF `in special education` THEN 0.085 ELSE 0.055

-- 15.8: minimum shekel amounts — class educator, the higher of 10% (11.5%
-- in first grade) and 1,000; grade coordinator and young-division head,
-- the higher of 7% (up to 4 classes) or 6% and 1,100; deputy, the higher of
-- 20% and 1,100 (printed "1.100").
@ref akn:art_15__para_15-8 akn:art_15__para_15-8__subpara_15-8-1 akn:art_15__para_15-8__subpara_15-8-1/p2 akn:art_15__para_15-8__subpara_15-8-1/p3
GIVEN `combined salary` IS A NUMBER, `first grade` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the class educator's bonus` `combined salary` `first grade` IS
    max ((IF `first grade` THEN 0.115 ELSE 0.1) TIMES `combined salary`) 1000

@ref akn:art_15__para_15-8__subpara_15-8-2 akn:art_15__para_15-8__subpara_15-8-2/p2 akn:art_15__para_15-8__subpara_15-8-2/p3 akn:art_15__para_15-8__subpara_15-8-3 akn:art_15__para_15-8__subpara_15-8-3/p2 akn:art_15__para_15-8__subpara_15-8-3/p3
GIVEN `combined salary` IS A NUMBER, `classes in the grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the grade coordinator's or young-division head's bonus` `combined salary` `classes in the grade` IS
    max ((IF `classes in the grade` AT MOST 4 THEN 0.07 ELSE 0.06) TIMES `combined salary`) 1100

@ref akn:art_15__para_15-8__subpara_15-8-4 akn:art_15__para_15-8__subpara_15-8-4/p2
GIVEN `combined salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the deputy's bonus` `combined salary` IS
    max (0.2 TIMES `combined salary`) 1100

§§ `16 גמול ליווי טיולים`

-- akn:art_16 The heading of section 16; no rule.

-- 16.1: under the agreement of 8.9.98, but only for hours beyond the
-- working hours of section 4.
@ref akn:art_16__para_16-1
GIVEN `activity hours` IS A NUMBER, `of them within working hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours the escort bonus is paid for` `activity hours` `of them within working hours` IS
    max (`activity hours` MINUS `of them within working hours`) 0

@desc One printed row of 16.2's table: when the activity ends (in hours of the day), and the bonus units.
DECLARE `escort band` HAS
    `band from hour` IS A NUMBER
    `band to hour`   IS A NUMBER
    `band units`     IS A NUMBER

-- 16.2's table: ending by 15:00, 0; 15:00-16:00, 0.5; 16:00-18:00, 1.5;
-- 18:00-21:00, 3; 21:00-24:00, 4.5; detached 16:00-24:00, 3; overnight, 6.5.
@ref akn:art_16__para_16-2 akn:art_16__para_16-2/p2 akn:art_16__para_16-2__subpara_a akn:art_16__para_16-2__subpara_a/p2 akn:art_16__para_16-2__subpara_a/p3 akn:art_16__para_16-2__subpara_a/p4 akn:art_16__para_16-2__subpara_a/p5 akn:art_16__para_16-2__subpara_a/p6
`the escort table by ending hour` MEANS
    LIST `escort band` 0  15 0,
         `escort band` 15 16 0.5,
         `escort band` 16 18 1.5,
         `escort band` 18 21 3,
         `escort band` 21 24 4.5

@ref akn:art_16__para_16-2__subpara_b akn:art_16__para_16-2__subpara_b/p2
`the units of a detached activity between 16:00 and 24:00` MEANS 3

@ref akn:art_16__para_16-2__subpara_c
`the units of an activity with an overnight stay` MEANS 6.5

GIVEN `ending hour` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the units the table gives for an end at` `ending hour` IS
    map (GIVEN b YIELD b's `band units`)
        (filter (GIVEN b YIELD `ending hour` AT LEAST b's `band from hour` AND `ending hour` AT MOST b's `band to hour`)
                `the escort table by ending hour`)

-- F-2023-24_tashpad_02-g: an end at 16:00, 18:00 or 21:00 is in two rows.
-- The reading adopted: a row includes its closing hour.
`the escort table gives an end at 16:00 two unit counts` MEANS
    `the units the table gives for an end at` 16 EQUALS LIST 0.5, 1.5
#ASSERT `the escort table gives an end at 16:00 two unit counts`

GIVEN `ending hour` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `escort units for an end at` `ending hour` IS
    BRANCH IF `ending hour` AT MOST 15 THEN 0
           IF `ending hour` AT MOST 16 THEN 0.5
           IF `ending hour` AT MOST 18 THEN 1.5
           IF `ending hour` AT MOST 21 THEN 3
           OTHERWISE 4.5

-- 16.3: a unit ("יחידת פעילות") is 0.7% of the monthly combined salary of
-- a full position.
@ref akn:art_16__para_16-3
GIVEN `units` IS A NUMBER, `full-position combined salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the escort bonus` `units` `full-position combined salary` IS
    `units` TIMES 0.007 TIMES `full-position combined salary`

-- 16.4: the hours paid to a teacher escorting on the day off or on a day of
-- fewer than 7 hours are paid at the reform's substitute-hour value: placed
-- for 0 hours, 7; for 1, 6; ... for 7 or more, 0 — or the activity's hours
-- if fewer.
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_02-h: it is not said whether these hours replace 16.2's
-- units or come on top. The reading adopted: on such a day 16.4 governs.
@ref akn:art_16__para_16-4 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p2 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p3 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p4 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p5 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p6 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p7 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p8 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p9 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p10 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p11 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p12 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p13 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p14 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p15 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p16 akn:art_16__para_16-4/p17
GIVEN `hours placed that day` IS A NUMBER, `activity hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `substitute hours paid for escorting` `hours placed that day` `activity hours` IS
    min (max (7 MINUS `hours placed that day`) 0) `activity hours`

GIVEN `hours placed that day` IS A NUMBER, `ending hour` IS A NUMBER, `activity hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the payments 16.2 and 16.4 name for one escort` `hours placed that day` `ending hour` `activity hours` IS
    LIST (`escort units for an end at` `ending hour`),
         (IF `hours placed that day` LESS THAN 7 THEN `substitute hours paid for escorting` `hours placed that day` `activity hours` ELSE 0)

`a short-day escort ending at 20:00 is named both units and hours` MEANS
    all (GIVEN x YIELD x GREATER THAN 0) (`the payments 16.2 and 16.4 name for one escort` 3 20 9)
#ASSERT `a short-day escort ending at 20:00 is named both units and hours`

§§ `17 מקדמות שכר באופק חדש עד לקביעת הדרגה`

-- akn:art_17 The heading of section 17; no rule.

@desc The current (non-reform) salary components 17.1 computes the advance on, for one month.
DECLARE `advance components` HAS
    `combined salary component`   IS A NUMBER
    `supplement 87`               IS A NUMBER
    `supplement 94`               IS A NUMBER
    `supplement 2001`             IS A NUMBER
    `supplement 2008`             IS A NUMBER
    `split-day bonus`             IS A NUMBER
    `in-service training bonuses` IS A NUMBER
    `double-degree bonus`         IS A NUMBER
    `supplement 2011`             IS A NUMBER

GIVEN c IS AN `advance components`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the advance base` c IS
    c's `combined salary component`
    PLUS c's `supplement 87`
    PLUS c's `supplement 94`
    PLUS c's `supplement 2001`
    PLUS c's `supplement 2008`
    PLUS c's `split-day bonus`
    PLUS c's `in-service training bonuses`
    PLUS c's `double-degree bonus`
    PLUS c's `supplement 2011`

DECLARE `advance group` IS ONE OF
    `primary, or grades 1-6 of a multi-stage school`
    `post-primary, or grades 7 and up of a multi-stage school`

-- 17.2: primary (and grades 1-6 of a multi-stage school): 14% for those who
-- are not principals or first deputies, interns included; post-primary (and
-- grades 7 and up): 20%, interns included; academic first deputies 17%,
-- academic principals 12%. ¶11: the reimbursement comes in a separate
-- circular.
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_02-i: no rate is set for a non-academic principal or
-- first deputy (9.11-9.12 employ them on the reform's terms). The reading
-- adopted: none is computed under this circular.
@ref akn:art_17__para_17-2 akn:art_17__para_17-2/p2 akn:art_17__para_17-2/p3 akn:art_17__para_17-2/p4 akn:art_17__para_17-2/p5 akn:art_17__para_17-2/p6 akn:art_17__para_17-2/p7 akn:art_17__para_17-2/p8 akn:art_17__para_17-2/p9 akn:art_17__para_17-2/p10 akn:art_17__para_17-2/p11
GIVEN r IS A `role`, `academic` IS A BOOLEAN, g IS AN `advance group`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the advance rate` r `academic` g IS
    IF r EQUALS `principal`
    THEN IF `academic` THEN JUST 0.12 ELSE NOTHING
    ELSE IF r EQUALS `first deputy principal`
         THEN IF `academic` THEN JUST 0.17 ELSE NOTHING
         ELSE CONSIDER g
              WHEN `primary, or grades 1-6 of a multi-stage school` THEN JUST 0.14
              WHEN `post-primary, or grades 7 and up of a multi-stage school` THEN JUST 0.2

`17.2 sets no advance rate for a non-academic manager` MEANS
        isNothing (`the advance rate` `principal` FALSE `primary, or grades 1-6 of a multi-stage school`)
    AND isNothing (`the advance rate` `first deputy principal` FALSE `primary, or grades 1-6 of a multi-stage school`)
#ASSERT `17.2 sets no advance rate for a non-academic manager`

-- 17.1: until the grade is set, the owner pays joined teachers an advance
-- ("מקדמת אופק חדש") on top of their current salary, on its listed
-- components, only for the part of the position in the joined school and
-- from joining; afterwards pay is recomputed back to joining and what was
-- paid, the advance included, is offset.
@ref akn:art_17__para_17-1 akn:art_17__para_17-1/p2 akn:art_17__para_17-1/p3
GIVEN r IS A `role`, `academic` IS A BOOLEAN, g IS AN `advance group`, c IS AN `advance components`, `share in the joined school` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Ofek Hadash advance` r `academic` g c `share in the joined school` IS
    CONSIDER `the advance rate` r `academic` g
    WHEN JUST rate THEN rate TIMES `the advance base` c TIMES `share in the joined school`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0

§§ `18 שעון הנוכחות בביה"ס`

-- akn:art_18 The heading of section 18; no rule.

-- 18.1, 18.3: an attendance clock is installed and teachers report by it;
-- until then, by hand.
@ref akn:art_18__para_18-1 akn:art_18__para_18-3
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 2 action`
DECIDE `the attendance clock` IS
    (PARTY `the local authority or owning body` MUST `install an attendance clock` WITHIN `31 August 2024`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the teaching employee` MUST `report hours by the attendance clock` WITHIN `31 August 2024`)

-- 18.2: hours count from clocking in, not before 7:45.
@ref akn:art_18__para_18-2
GIVEN `clock-in time` IS A NUMBER @desc in hours of the day, 7.75 is 7:45
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours count from` `clock-in time` IS
    max `clock-in time` 7.75

-- 18.4: the owner pays and deducts by the clock's reports, after checking
-- approvals of justified absence.
@ref akn:art_18__para_18-4
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 2 action`
DECIDE `pay by the attendance reports` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `pay and deduct by the attendance reports`
    WITHIN `31 August 2024`
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "circular תשפ\"ד/2 18.4: the owner pays and deducts by the attendance clock's reports"

DECLARE `source` IS ONE OF
    `this circular`
    `the collective agreements`

-- 18.4 ¶2-¶3 (the circular's closing paragraphs, which the corpus files
-- under 18.4): the circular gathers the agreements' rules; in a conflict,
-- for or against the employee, the agreements govern.
@ref akn:art_18__para_18-4/p2 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p3
GIVEN `the circular and the agreements conflict` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `source`
DECIDE `which governs` `the circular and the agreements conflict` IS
    IF `the circular and the agreements conflict` THEN `the collective agreements` ELSE `this circular`

-- akn:art_18__para_18-4/p4 A pointer to the addresses in annex ה; no rule.
-- akn:art_18__para_18-4/p5 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p6 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p7 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p8 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p9 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p10 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p11 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p12 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p13 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p14 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p15 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p16 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p17 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p18 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p19 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p20 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p21 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p22 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p23 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p24 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p25 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p26 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p27 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p28 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p29 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p30 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p31 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p32 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p33 akn:art_18__para_18-4/p34 The sign-off, signatories and list of copies, which the corpus files under 18.4; no rule.

§§ `נספח א' — כתב התחייבות`

-- annex א ¶1-¶8: the owner's signatory quotes regulation 3(6) as amended and
-- commits, from תשפ"ד, to apply to the teachers of its listed
-- special-education schools all the Ofek Hadash agreement's provisions that
-- concern a special-education school (work week, pay, pedagogic guidance),
-- knowing that breach may bring sanctions up to revocation of the licence.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 akn:att_1__hc_1/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1/p3 akn:att_1__hc_1/p4 akn:att_1__hc_1/p5 akn:att_1__hc_1/p6 akn:att_1__hc_1/p7 akn:att_1__hc_1/p8
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 2 action`
DECIDE `the owner's commitment` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `apply the Ofek Hadash agreement`
    WITHIN `1 September 2023`
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "annex א: breach of the commitment may bring sanctions up to revocation of the licence"

-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p9 akn:att_1__hc_1/p10 akn:att_1__hc_1/p11 akn:att_1__hc_1/p12 akn:att_1__hc_1/p13 akn:att_1__hc_1/p14 akn:att_1__hc_1/p15 akn:att_1__hc_1/p16 The signature block and date lines of the commitment, and the next page's letterhead; no rule.

§§ `נספחים ב'-ג' — טפסים`

-- akn:att_2__hc_1 Annex ב, the form for an academic teacher to join by exception: details, the year, and the acknowledgements 3.2 and 13.2.2 encode; sent by e-mail. No rule of its own.
-- akn:att_3__hc_1 Annex ג, the form for a request to the exceptions committee to leave Ofek Hadash; sent by e-mail (section 11 encodes the rule). No rule of its own.

§§ `נספח ד' — קביעת דרגה והמרות שכר`

-- ¶1-¶5: an existing teacher's grade is set by converting the salary; a new
-- teacher starts at grade 1 by education and role without conversion; the
-- Ministry alone sets grades.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1/p1 akn:att_4__hc_1/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1/p3 akn:att_4__hc_1/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1/p5
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 2 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the salary is converted` t IF
    `is an existing teaching employee` t

-- The erosion supplement the deputy's and principal's examples multiply by.
`the erosion supplement` MEANS 0.034

-- 1א (and 2א, 3א): A = X × (100 + Y) / 100.
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_02-j: the formula has no erosion supplement; the
-- deputy's and principal's conversion examples apply one, and the
-- principal's personal-supplement example does not. The reading adopted:
-- the conversion examples' method for A, and B as defined.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p5 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p6
GIVEN X IS A NUMBER, Y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary after conversion by the formula` X Y IS
    X TIMES (100 PLUS Y) DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN X IS A NUMBER, Y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary after conversion as the examples compute it` X Y IS
    X TIMES (1 PLUS `the erosion supplement`) TIMES (100 PLUS Y) DIVIDED BY 100

-- 1ב ¶2-¶6: X for a teacher — the salary due at 100% by the roles held in
-- March of the year before the move (or the joining month), on the listed
-- components and the role bonuses that do not survive the reform.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p5 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p6
GIVEN `components at 100% in March` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a teacher's salary for conversion` `components at 100% in March` IS
    sum `components at 100% in March`

-- akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p7 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p8 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p9 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p10 The next page's letterhead; no rule.

-- 1ב ¶11-¶14: the academic coefficients (the page's table, not in the
-- corpus, so an input); non-academics with 28 years or more × 0.8; grades
-- 7-9 of a primary school on a 24-hour base "grow by 12.5%".
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_02-k: 12.5% of itself, or 12.5 points. The reading
-- adopted: 12.5 points.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p11 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p12 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p13 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p14
GIVEN `academic coefficient` IS A NUMBER @desc Y for an academic teacher of this status, in percent, from the page's table of academic coefficients (not in the corpus)
      `academic`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `grades 7-9 on a 24-hour base` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the conversion coefficient` `academic coefficient` `academic` `grades 7-9 on a 24-hour base` IS
    (IF `academic` THEN `academic coefficient` ELSE `academic coefficient` TIMES 0.8)
    PLUS (IF `grades 7-9 on a 24-hour base` THEN 12.5 ELSE 0)

GIVEN `academic coefficient` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the coefficient grown by 12.5% of itself` `academic coefficient` IS
    `academic coefficient` TIMES 1.125

`the two readings of 12.5% differ` MEANS
    NOT (`the conversion coefficient` 24 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the coefficient grown by 12.5% of itself` 24)
#ASSERT `the two readings of 12.5% differ`

-- 1ב ¶15-¶18: the formula again; A is placed in the table by education and
-- seniority, at the grade of the higher but nearest salary.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p15 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p16 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p17 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p18
GIVEN `A` IS A NUMBER, `salaries of the grades at this seniority` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the placed salary` `A` `salaries of the grades at this seniority` IS
    minimum (filter (GIVEN s YIELD s AT LEAST `A`) `salaries of the grades at this seniority`)

-- 1ב ¶19 and points 1-5 (points 3-4 repeat 1-2, and ¶2 of point 2 repeats
-- the heading "דגשים"): new academics start at grade 1, seniority 1,
-- without conversion; one on unpaid absence in the year before joining is
-- converted on September's salary of the year of the move; the 2016 shekel
-- and Ofek 2022 supplements are due on top.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p19 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_1 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_5
GIVEN `absent without pay in the year before joining` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the month the conversion salary is taken from` `absent without pay in the year before joining` IS
    IF `absent without pay in the year before joining`
    THEN "September of the year of the move"
    ELSE "March of the year before the move"

-- 2א-2ג: a first deputy, Y = 20%; X without educator bonus, expense refunds,
-- sundry payments, grossing-up and imputation, at 100%, in March of the
-- year before (September of the move if then absent).
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_b akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_b/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p3
`the first deputy's coefficient` MEANS 20

GIVEN `components paid by the position` IS A NUMBER, `components paid at 100%` IS A NUMBER, `position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a manager's salary for conversion` `components paid by the position` `components paid at 100%` `position` IS
    `components paid by the position` DIVIDED BY `position` PLUS `components paid at 100%`

