-- 3ה ¶5-¶17: for the position above 100% up to 140%, a personal
-- supplement: B = T × (100 + Y) / 100, T the full salary by the position in
-- March of the year before (or before the absence); C = B − the new table
-- salary, as a percentage of the combined salary.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p5 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p6 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p7 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p8 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p9 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p10 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p11 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p12 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p13 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p14 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p15 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p16 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p17
GIVEN T IS A NUMBER, Y IS A NUMBER, `new table salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the personal supplement` T Y `new table salary` IS
    `rounded to the agora` ((T TIMES (100 PLUS Y)) DIVIDED BY 100)
    MINUS `new table salary`

-- 3ה 1-4: the example — T = 20,735.13; × 1.15 = 23,845.4; C = 3,758.72;
-- 18.712%.
